WEBVTT

00:00:10.961 --> 00:00:16.843
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <i>There are two types of twins: non-identical twins, who don’t look the same,</i>

00:00:17.089 --> 00:00:21.340
<i>and identical twins, who look exactly the same.</i>

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:29.200
<i>But did you know that there are also ‘twin strangers’ – people who look the same,</i>

00:00:29.385 --> 00:00:31.460
<i>but are not related at all?</i>

00:00:32.889 --> 00:00:39.993
<i>They say we all have seven twin strangers in the world – seven people who are not our relatives,</i>

00:00:40.089 --> 00:00:43.060
<i>but who look nearly identical to us.</i>

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:51.270
<i>On the twentieth of March twenty fifteen, three friends from Dublin began a unique challenge.</i>

00:00:51.665 --> 00:00:52.483
<v><b>Niamh:</b></v> Hi, I’m Niamh.

00:00:52.651 --> 00:00:53.241
<v><b>Terence:</b></v> I’m Terence.

00:00:53.241 --> 00:00:53.993
<v><b>Harry:</b></v> And I’m Harry.

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:57.200
<v><b>Niamh:</b></v> And we’re trying to find our twin strangers from anywhere in the world.

00:00:58.481 --> 00:01:01.835
<v><b>Harry:</b></v> Basically, we’ve set ourselves a challenge and we have one month,

00:01:01.835 --> 00:01:05.571
starting from today, erm, to find people that look really, really like us

00:01:05.571 --> 00:01:07.670
or almost completely identical.

00:01:08.244 --> 00:01:12.243
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <i>The three friends advertised their project on social media.</i>

00:01:13.003 --> 00:01:19.560
<i>Soon messages and photos started coming in from everywhere in the world, especially for Niamh.</i>

00:01:20.857 --> 00:01:24.220
<i>After two weeks, Niamh got to meet Karen,</i>

00:01:24.465 --> 00:01:27.406
<i>the first of her potential twin strangers.</i>

00:01:28.113 --> 00:01:30.580
<i>It was a very exciting meeting.</i>

00:01:31.115 --> 00:01:38.460
<i>Niamh and Karen decided to put on the same make-up and do their hair the same way for a photo.</i>

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.299
<v><b>Niamh:</b></v> So guys, this is it – make-up and hair, what do you think?

00:01:55.934 --> 00:02:00.060
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <i>Niamh continued to search for her other six Twin Strangers,</i>

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.305
<i>and she found number two...in Italy!</i>

00:02:04.535 --> 00:02:08.512
<v><b>Niamh:</b></v> There’s this lovely girl named Luisa that got in touch on the site so

00:02:08.537 --> 00:02:11.340
I had this crazy idea – why not go fly and meet her?

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.740
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <i>So Niamh travelled to Genoa on the Italian Riviera.</i>

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.120
<v><b>Niamh:</b></v> It’s so great to meet you and meet your face!

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:22.940
<v><b>Narrator:</b></v> <i>So, what about the boys?</i>

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.686
<i>Harry found two or three people like him,</i>

00:02:26.897 --> 00:02:29.920
<i>but they weren’t as good as Niamh’s ‘twin strangers’.</i>

00:02:31.134 --> 00:02:37.540
<i>Terence received some photos, mainly from the USA, but they weren’t very like him.</i>

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:43.740
<i>He says, ‘I think there are definitely Black guys out there who look like me.’</i>

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:48.780
<i>Soon their online project became a website,</i>

00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:55.110
<i>and since then many people have found their ‘twin’ on twinstrangers.com.</i>

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:02.350
<i>Sara, from Sweden, found Shannon, from Ireland, after they both went on the site,</i>

00:03:02.468 --> 00:03:04.064
<i>and they met in Dublin.</i>

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.980
<i>So, if you’d like to meet your twin stranger,</i>

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:15.060
<i>all you need to do is go to their website, upload a photo, and… who knows?</i>

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:20.540
<i>In a few days’ time, you might find someone who looks just like you!</i>